WEBVTT

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.896
Another one was
on the photoelectric effect,

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.280
that's why solar panels work,
it's a nice one.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.496
Gave him the Nobel prize for that one.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.656
And the fourth introduced an equation
you might have heard of:

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.976
E equals mc squared.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.576
So, tell me again how you
shouldn't do several things at once.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.976
Now, obviously, working simultaneously

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.896
on Brownian motion, special relativity
and the photoelectric effect --

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.456
it's not exactly the same
kind of multitasking

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.096
as Snapchatting while
you're watching "Westworld."

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.576
Very different.